61686	Q0	zis182	9	1.8157374	instruments_tools	The AR1 is a highly economic scale for measuring physical attractiveness. Furthermore the AR1 allows a measurement of the construct in which the usual confounding influences are largely controlled by features of the evaluators such as their age and gender. The scale can be administered in different computer assisted survey modes.
61686	Q0	zis298	10	1.7404608	instruments_tools	The Luxembourg Workplace Mobbing Scale LWMS is a very brief five item unidimensional instrument to assess workplace mobbing exposure in the general working population. It was validated in three different language versions German French Luxembourgish . Using data collected via computer assisted telephone interviews in representative samples of Luxembourgish employees two studies Steffgen et al. 2019 Sischka et al. 2020 confirmed its reliability factor structure construct and criterion validity as well as partial scalar invariance across language age gender and occupational groups. Due to its briefness while at the same time being robust against language age gender and occupational group factors and exhibiting meaningful criterion validity the LWMS is particularly attractive for large scale surveys.
61686	Q0	zis114	11	1.5930486	instruments_tools	The instrument is one of eight item batteries that Lederer used as subscales to capture various aspects of attitudes to authority. This subscale is used to record attitudes to loyalty to the state and patriotism.
61686	Q0	zis230	12	1.5862681	instruments_tools	The NFC K measures the expression of the Need for Cognition NFC construct with four items that reflect two facets of the construct engagement and joy . The capture of the construct NFC plays an important role in larger surveys of different content areas especially as a control variable. The NFC short scale enables an objective reliable and valid measurement and is economically applicable. The scale can be used for people from adolescence onwards as the metacognitive skills necessary for assessment are developed during adolescence Oerter Dreher 2002 .
61686	Q0	zis115	13	1.5640256	instruments_tools	The instrument is one of eight item batteries that Lederer used as subscales to capture various aspects of attitudes to authority. The aim is to record attitudes to one s own parents and to parental authority in general.
61686	Q0	sg-13	14	1.5547241	instruments_tools	Interviewers affect survey estimates in three ways They play a major role in the response rate that is achieved they are responsible for training and motivating respondents and they must handle their part of the interview interaction and question and answer process in a standardized nonbiasing way Fowler 2014 110 . Survey techniques that require the use of interviewers necessarily presuppose the recruitment and training of these staff. Regardless of whether potential interviewers are to conduct face to face or telephone interviews they play one of the two key roles in the interview situation namely to motivate the target person to participate in the survey and to collect data within the framework of the interview. Because the interviewer influences the respondent s willingness to participate and his response behaviour it must be ensured that this influence is on track . Hence to minimise interviewer effects special attention should be paid to the selection training and motivation of the interviewers as the quality of the fieldwork and thus the quality of the data depends decisively on the participating actors. Thus the optimisation of data quality begins with the selection of the interviewers continues during interviewer training and ends with interviewer monitoring. The present contribution addresses the following questions What should be taken into consideration when recruiting interviewers What type of training should be conducted What quality assurance and quality control measures can be implemented
61686	Q0	zis117	15	1.5452576	instruments_tools	The instrument is one of eight item batteries that Lederer used as subscales to capture various aspects of attitudes to authority. This subscale is intended to record young people s attitudes to their own parents and to parental authority in general.
61686	Q0	zis192	16	1.5360414	instruments_tools	With eight items this scale measures attitudes to the services and functions of the welfare and welfare state. The attitudes towards the welfare state are to be regarded as indicators for social value orientations which can be seen as a subjective evaluation of the social structure.
61686	Q0	zis136	17	1.5134108	instruments_tools	This scale serves to capture the generalized attitude to education which like the construct of idealistic educational aspiration refers to the strength of a positive attitude to education and to the extent to which higher educational attainment is seen as an indispensable necessity. The underlying theory is the model of frame selection in which educational decisions are based 1 on global and schematically ordered attitudes and 2 on respondents values. The answers thus express the extent to which a higher level of education is regarded as a value in itself.
61686	Q0	zis143	18	1.5090408	instruments_tools	This instrument uses seven items to record attitudes towards perceptions of the authenticity or credibility of typical asylum applications as well as attitudes towards appropriate political dealings with asylum seekers. Data from six European countries were used for the construction.
61686	Q0	zis11	19	1.4829731	instruments_tools	The questionnaire shows the three areas 1 career orientation 2 performance and success enhancing work attitudes and 3 fear of failure. The items were formulated in order to reflect performance related attitude and behaviour symptoms in the interviewee s self perception or self reflection.
61686	Q0	zis6	20	1.4744829	instruments_tools	The seven instruments for recording socio political activities and attitudes developed by scientists from the Social Science Institute of the Federal Armed Forces SOWI relate to these areas Political Alienation Social Isolation Politics as a Disruptive Factor Apolitical Attitudes Power of Disposal Political Commitment and Anomie.
61686	Q0	zis157	21	1.4660892	instruments_tools	The items documented here capture attitudes to specific foreign groups as well as to foreign nations and cultures in general. Accepting responses to their items affirm a threat experienced by foreign groups and their values and norms and express a suspicious and negative attitude towards them and their integration into one s own society.
61686	Q0	zis224	22	1.4296424	instruments_tools	The scale records attitudes towards foreigners with four items and is regularly used in the ALLBUS.
61686	Q0	zis310	23	1.426854	instruments_tools	The MCGM G is the German adaptation of the Multi Component Gratitude Measure MCGM . This measurement was originally developed by Morgen et al. 2017 . The instrument encompasses attitudinal and behavioral aspects of gratitude. The validation was conducted via an online survey with a sample of N 508 participants. The MCGM G has good internal consistency and both construct and criterion validity are established. In addition there is partial cultural scalar invariance with the English version Morgan et al. 2017 for five dimensions. In addition the MCGM G is scalar invariant across gender.
61686	Q0	zis10	24	1.3835611	instruments_tools	The OCQ measures the affective loyalty of employees to their organisation. The OCQ is based on the conceptualisation of organisational commitment as an affective attitude.
61686	Q0	zis231	25	1.3835611	instruments_tools	The scale measures attitudes to Islam in Germany and was used in the General Population Survey of the Social Sciences ALLBUS in 2012.
61686	Q0	zis291	26	1.3829956	instruments_tools	The High Performance Team Survey HPTS captures major success factors of high performing teams. Based on the insights generated by Google s team study Project Aristotle and major findings from international team research five different psychological characteristics of successful teamwork are included in the survey psychological safety dependability high performance standards structure clarity of roles plans and goals meaningfulness of work impact on the organization. There are three different versions of the HPTS long medium and short version all of which show very good psychometric properties. For all three version substantial correlations with other constructs point to the construct and criterion validity of the HPTS.
61686	Q0	zis121	27	1.3723435	instruments_tools	The two items documented here are intended to measure 1 trust or mistrust in other people with three indicators each and 2 the assessment of general social morality or nature. According to the theory of the Berkeley Group strongly negative attitudes towards these questions are part of a central characteristic syndrome of an authoritarian personality for which a stable cynical moralizing and pejorative attitude towards others across situations is characteristic.
61686	Q0	zis97	28	1.3688539	instruments_tools	The items documented here were used to measure the ALLBUS 96 theme Attitudes towards ethnic groups in Germany .
61686	Q0	zis168	29	1.313024	instruments_tools	The scale Littering Environmental Aesthetics ILU records attitudes behavioural readiness and self reported behaviours from the topic of throwing away waste outdoors.
