45793	Q0	zis257	2	2.3810337	instruments_tools	The questionnaire for determining the Occupational and Organisational Climate Index BOKX maps the two dimensions meaning and competence with four items each. The BOKX serves as a short screening instrument to record the expression of these two psychological states of experience. Experiencing meaning and competence is considered a personal resource and thus an important prerequisite for health well being and performance.
45793	Q0	dbd-23	3	1.4760897	instruments_tools	This guide is written for readers who want to get familiar with the academic use of web tracking as a method for studying digital media use and online behavior. It addresses researchers students and practitioners in the social sciences including political science media and communication research sociology and computational social science who are interested in how web tracking data collections differ from other digital research methods and how web tracking data can be used to analyze individual level behaviors in online environments. The guide introduces the conceptual foundations of web tracking outlines its methodological advantages and discusses key technical ethical and legal challenges. It also provides an overview of practical implementation steps including software development participant recruitment and data processing. Throughout this guide examples informed by existing research illustrate how web tracking can be leveraged to study a wide range of topics such as political communication and news use health information seeking or climate change communication.
81	Q0	zis195	0	3.554887	instruments_tools	The items documented here capture the family climate in the perception of young people in five subscales the positive emotional climate PEK active leisure activities AFK organisation ORG control KON and intellectual cultural orientation IKO . They thus operationalise an economic recording of the family climate perceived by young people.
