81	Q0	zis223	2	2.6018076	instruments_tools	Due to their importance for any society gender role attitudes have been included in surveys of special groups and the entire population for several decades. In accordance to the changed opportunity structure behavior of women changed too. The question was then whether the changed opportunity structure for women their changed behavior and the women s movement had also produced changes in attitudes. The documented items acquire gender role attitudes in three dimensions. The Consequence dimension C the Gender role ideology dimension G and the Economic consequences dimension E . The first and the second dimension include four items while the last dimension includes three.
