4472	Q0	zis174	20	1.1452072	instruments_tools	With five items the scale measures the development of a global personal norm for environmentally friendly behavior. The development of the scale is based on the works of Schwartz 1977 1981 .
4472	Q0	zis344	21	1.1363919	instruments_tools	The GRowing Work Inventory GR W I is a validated German language instrument to measure the construct of positive growth employee thrivng . In accordance with Spreitzer et al. 2005 positive growth refers to the extent to which employees can literally thrive and flourish at work. The GR W I comprises the two constructs energy and learning. The GR W I shows good psychometric properties. Substantial correlations with related constructs are indicators for convergent construct validity and criterion and incremental validity of the instrument.
4472	Q0	gml-23	22	1.1336479	instruments_tools	These files add derived innovation concepts variables to Eurostat CIS Community Innovation Survey 3 4 2006 and 2008 data. Works for SPSS and Stata.
4472	Q0	zis133	23	1.1336479	instruments_tools	The questionnaire measures the tendency to postpone rewards. The development of the scale is based on the work of Utz 1979 whose original 20 items were reduced to 12 by Blass.
4472	Q0	zis175	24	1.1336479	instruments_tools	With six items the scale measures the development of a specific personal norm for environmentally friendly behavior in traffic. The development of the scale is based on the works of Schwartz 1977 1981 .
4472	Q0	zis73	25	1.1223197	instruments_tools	The questionnaire records the tendency to search for experience and risk motivation. From this the two subscales news and intensity can be formed. The development of the scale is based on the work of Arnett 1994 .
4472	Q0	zis59	26	1.1112157	instruments_tools	The questionnaire captures the need for evaluation. v. Collani divides the construct into the two factors need for evaluation and need for neutrality . The development of the scale is based on the work of Jarvis and Petty 1996 .
