2272	Q0	zis290_exz	37	1.1320008	instruments_tools	The ASKU is an economic instrument for recording individual competence expectations to be able to deal with difficulties and obstacles in daily life. It was originally developed and validated in German by Beierlein Kemper Kovaleva Rammstedt 2013 . In 2019 we developed and tested a French Version of this scale and tested it for reliability internal consistency validity and measurement equivalence towards the original German Version see D cieux et al. 2020 .The provided evidence on the quality of the German and the French Version of ASKU FASKU indicates that the scales allow a reliable valid and economic assessment of subjective competence expectations and that the two language versions can be used to assess and compare self efficacy in German and French speaking populations.
2272	Q0	zis73	38	1.1223197	instruments_tools	The questionnaire records the tendency to search for experience and risk motivation. From this the two subscales news and intensity can be formed. The development of the scale is based on the work of Arnett 1994 .
2272	Q0	zis59	39	1.1112157	instruments_tools	The questionnaire captures the need for evaluation. v. Collani divides the construct into the two factors need for evaluation and need for neutrality . The development of the scale is based on the work of Jarvis and Petty 1996 .
2272	Q0	zis343	40	1.1037136	instruments_tools	Respondents age is together with sex gender the most important socio demographic variable recorded in all surveys. Age provides information about partly biologically determined development and ageing processes and positioning in the life course. It is therefore related to a variety of socio economic characteristics but also to attitudes behaviour and in particular health. It is controlled for in practically all multivariate statistical models. In most studies the age at the time of the survey is determined using questions on the month and year of birth and published as a derived variable. Membership in a birth cohort is also derived from the year of birth. It is used to depict similar overall social living conditions and experiences that lead to the construction of generations e.g. the post war generation or the baby boomers .
2272	Q0	gml-24	41	1.1003293	instruments_tools	These filee merge and harmonize the Eurostat CIS Community Innovation Survey 3 4 2006 and 2008 country level files adds weights and harmonizes NACE. Works for SPSS and Stata.
